t until you unlock.␀␀␀␀Set passphrase␀␀Coming from the Lua app␀Moves its pads here with their counters, so you carry on in step with the other side. Afterwards remove the Lua app: two apps using one pad would burn the same bytes twice.␀␀␀␀Move pads from the Lua app␀␀20261012.native-1␀␀␀OTP Messenger %s В· wire-compatible with OTP_3_RC1 and MeshCore Open TAK␀␀␀␀Everything wiped. Protection is off.␀␀␀␀Wrong passphrase␀␀␀␀Too many conversations␀␀ (manual)␀␀␀%d B (max)␀␀%d B (QR-safe)␀␀Channel pad, shared by everyone on it␀␀␀One-time pad␀␀␀␀B left of %u␀␀␀␀Role %c%s  В·  sent %u B  В·  received %u B␀Offset %u  В·  shared by everyone on #%s␀␀␀␀Sync:␀␀␀not checked yet␀%d message(s) waiting for a path␀␀␀␀Open chat␀␀␀Check sync␀␀Add pad bytes␀␀␀Size to generate␀␀␀␀Generate %d random bytes␀␀␀␀Import a file from the SD card␀␀Paste hex␀␀␀Add text␀␀␀␀Share␀␀␀Show as QR code␀Check code␀␀Play the check code␀оЉѓ␀Listen for a check code␀Export to the SD card␀␀␀о…–␀Flip role␀␀␀Check code: the same on both devices means the same pad. Read it out, or play it by sound (Sound link) and listen on the other one; it reveals nothing about the pad.␀␀␀Show as QR code: MeshCore Open TAK scans it from its OTP Pad screen (Scan QR), a few parts in turn. Export writes this pad, unused, to the SD card as hex. The other device imports the same file; roles A/B are worked out from your keys, so both sides import it unchanged.␀␀Danger zone␀Cancel waiting messages␀Wipe pad␀␀␀␀Delete conversation␀Pad wiped␀␀␀Imported %d bytes␀␀␀Delete the file when both sides have it.␀␀␀␀File deleted.␀␀␀Could not open the file␀File too large for a pad␀␀␀␀Imported %s. %s␀No OTP pads from the Lua app found␀␀Moved %d pad(s), counters included. Remove the Lua app so only one copy is used.␀␀␀␀Nothing to move: those pads are already here, or their contacts are unknown␀Lua app passphrase␀␀The Lua app's pads are protected. Its passphrase unlocks them once, to move them.␀␀␀Passphrases did not match␀␀␀Protection on. Pads and messages are now encrypted.␀Could not enable protection␀Added %d random bytes (hardware RNG)␀␀␀␀Added %d random bytes: the pad is now at the %d byte cap␀␀␀␀The pad is at the %d byte cap␀␀␀Contact␀[SOUND] heard %u bytes
␀Team setup: heard %d of %d␀␀Pad check heard: unlock OTP Messenger to compare it␀Same pad on both sides:␀Different pad for␀␀␀Share it again.␀%s %s: %lu / %lu B. %s␀␀Different pad bytes for␀Share it again before using it.␀No pad here matches that check code␀channel/add␀contact/add␀Channel:␀␀␀␀Contact:␀␀␀␀E:␀␀XOR:␀␀␀␀AES:␀␀␀␀(encrypted: set the passkey)␀␀␀␀%s%s: %s␀␀␀␀Couldn't post to the channel␀␀␀␀Sound link:␀Experimental. Slows the processor while the screen is off (Bluetooth and Wi-Fi keep working), lets the GPS rest between position checks and keeps a moving background still.␀␀␀␀Experimental␀␀␀␀Sends an extra copy of each ACK, so the sender is likelier to hear one.␀Multi ACKs␀␀Forwards other nodes' packets, like a repeater. Costs airtime and battery.␀␀Client repeat␀␀␀A little more receive sensitivity for a little more current.␀␀␀␀RX boosted gain␀Bluetooth pairing isn't available on this device. The radio chip's factory firmware doesn't support it.␀Pair the phone app over Wi-Fi instead: join this device to your network, then add it in the app by its IP address (TCP, port 5000), shown on the Wi-Fi page. USB works too.␀Enable Bluetooth␀␀␀␀Mode: BLE on (+ Wi-Fi)␀␀Mode: BLE on␀␀␀␀Mode: BLE starting / low memory␀Mode: BLE off (Wi-Fi on)␀␀␀␀Mode: BLE off␀␀␀Phone app␀␀␀%06lu␀␀␀------␀␀Pairing code␀␀␀␀Type a new 6-digit code В· applies after a reboot␀␀␀Battery & power history␀remote view open␀␀␀␀Battery saver␀␀␀Calibrate as full␀␀␀Tap with a full battery to call its voltage 100%. Hold to go back to the default.␀␀␀No sensors on this device.␀␀Ridge at six?␀␀␀On my way␀␀␀Apply and restart␀␀␀Red light␀␀␀Everything in dim red, the map and photos too, to keep your eyes used to the dark.␀␀Red light (night vision)␀␀␀␀Black and white with heavy outlines, for bright sun or low vision.␀␀Accent colour␀␀␀Colour␀␀A colour for every section, coloured status icons, names and glyphs in their own hue.␀␀␀MORE COLORS!␀␀␀␀Every app and page its own colour, with a little motion.␀␀␀␀Taste the rainbow␀␀␀Background␀␀Choose the colour␀␀␀оѓ¶␀Widgets, cards and panel tiles let the background show through. Off: solid tiles.␀␀␀Glass tiles␀Chat icons␀␀Names are always in colour; this colours the bubbles too.␀␀␀Colourful bubbles␀␀␀Compact messages (IRC style)␀␀␀␀Locking␀The touchscreen ignores taps until you unlock.␀␀Lock when screen off␀␀␀␀Off shows who wrote and how many, not what.␀Message text on lock screen␀PIN lock␀␀␀␀Asks for 4 numbers or letters to unlock, and locks whenever the screen goes off. If you forget it, the only way back in is to reset the device, which erases everything on it.␀␀Change PIN␀␀Export␀␀Export backup␀␀␀Off reuses meshcore-backup.json, the file name the MeshCore app uses.␀␀␀Append timestamp␀␀␀␀Saved to the SD card when one is in, otherwise to internal storage.␀Import backup␀␀␀Replaces identity, channels and contacts with the backup's, then restarts.␀␀Saved backups␀␀␀No backups yet. Use Export backup above to create one.␀␀Factory reset␀␀␀Erases identity, contacts, channels, messages, Wi-Fi and all settings, then reboots.␀␀␀␀Tap a language; the device reboots to apply.␀␀␀␀What each installed app is allowed to do. Anything an app sends goes out under your node name and cannot be told apart from a message you typed. Private covers direct messages and room posts, and is kept separate from channels on purpose. Turn one off to take it back.␀␀␀␀No apps installed.␀␀Post to channels as me␀␀Read channel messages␀␀␀Send private messages as me␀Read private messages␀␀␀Send discovery probes␀␀␀Not asked yet␀␀␀Keep holding: settings␀␀п”™  ␀␀␀пЂ‡  ␀␀␀пЃ№  ␀␀␀*  Unfav␀␀␀␀*  Favorite␀пЂЊ  Unblock␀␀␀␀пЃ№  Join␀␀␀пѓ   Open chat␀␀пЂ“  Admin␀␀пЂЎ  Ping␀␀␀пѓ   Message␀␀␀␀п‰Ѓ  Telemetry␀␀п„¤  Show on map␀␀␀␀п„¤  Hound␀␀п„¤  Trace SNR␀␀п‡«  Range test␀п„¤  Sightline␀␀пЊ„  Nickname␀␀␀п„¤  Stop sharing loc␀␀␀п„¤  Share my loc␀␀␀пЃ№  Reset path␀п‚“  Share contact␀␀Unfavorite it first␀Not in your contacts␀␀␀␀Self  %.4f, %.4f␀␀␀␀пѓ ␀Team: pick the team channel in Team